# FORMAT.md's ANCESTRY, recorded so drift can be detected rather than noticed.
#
# §C says FORMAT.md is normative and lives here. That is a claim about
# AUTHORITY, not about origin: the file was taken from the upstream project
# that defines the format, and until now nothing recorded which version of it
# this copy corresponds to. Upstream moved once already -- gaining §R RESEARCH,
# sectioned ownership and the right-size rule -- and this repo learned about it
# by someone asking, not by any check.
#
# TWO CHECKS READ THIS FILE, deliberately split by whether they need a network.
#
#   * `format-upstream` in hk.pkl -- OFFLINE. Asserts FORMAT.md still hashes to
#     `sha256` below, so editing the format means updating this record in the
#     same commit. The gate never reaches the network (see the `links` step),
#     so it cannot ask whether upstream changed, and does not pretend to.
#
#   * `.github/workflows/format-upstream.yml` -- ONLINE, weekly, and NOT part
#     of the gate. Fetches upstream's current FORMAT.md and compares. It fails
#     its own scheduled run and never a pull request: whether upstream moved
#     has nothing to do with the change under review, and a check that fails
#     unrelated PRs is one people learn to ignore.
#
# WHEN THEY DISAGREE, that is information, not an error. This copy is allowed
# to lead upstream, follow it, or fork from it -- what it may not do is differ
# without anyone knowing which. Update `rev` and `sha256` together, in the
# commit that makes the decision.
