# WHAT THIS COPY LEADS WITH, and where the proposal for it stands.
#
# `rev` and `sha256` above answer "which upstream version is this file". They
# cannot answer "and what do we enforce that it does not", because the answer
# is not in FORMAT.md by construction -- V8 keeps the vendored bytes
# unmodified and puts the superset in §V. FORMAT-EXTENSIONS.md is that
# superset rendered for a reader; this is where its UPSTREAM STATUS lives.
#
# Three outcomes, each legal, because §C asks only that the state be KNOWN:
# ACCEPTED means re-sync at the new rev and the extension leaves the document;
# DECLINED means this copy leads and the record says so; SILENCE means the
# same, dated from when it started, so nobody has to guess whether it was ever
# sent.
